{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/477670-scions-have-you-ever-statted-them-for-your-games","id":477670,"title":"Scions; have you ever statted them for your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-12T02:13:15-07:00","id":477670,"title":"Scions; have you ever statted them for your games?","content":"Pretty much what the title says. I know scions, the Disquiet-immune children of prometheans, are basically a storyteller's tool, but I'm wondering if anyone has ever mechanically supported scionhood in their games. Myself, I tend to treat it as a unique Supernatural Merit that combines Unseen Sense (Prometheans/Pyros) with &quot;immunity to Disquiet&quot;, as well as being a supernatural merit that can survive templatehood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:15:38-07:00","id":478748,"title":"","content":"Well I never got that far, but in first edition I'd have treated them like a minor template- making them the wolfblooded/sleepwalker equivalent.<br /> <br /> Instead of making it a supernatural merit, I'd suggest a cleaner approach- It's a template of extremely limited utility that is compatible with other templates, like 2d ed wolfblooded. <br /> <br /> Not only is making it a supernatural template messy because you don't get to keep those, but it implies that the god-machine can retroactively make one of your parents a promethean when it rewires your brain, or that a member of the ordo dracul will soon be able to learn how to be a scion.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the god-machine can't retroactively make someone's parent a promethean but it would have nothing to do with making them a stigmatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}